## Project Identity
- This is the **Rates** monorepo: a Firebase-backed financial accounts SPA for tracking accounts, payment periods, and amortization; plus a separate auth SPA for login + token validation.
- Tech stack (one line): **React 18 + Vite 6 + TypeScript 5 (strict) + Firebase (Auth/Firestore/Storage) + Tailwind CSS** in a pnpm workspace.
- Language/paradigm: **TypeScript**, functional/immutable-leaning style, **React hooks + functional components** (no class components).
- Styling: **Tailwind CSS is the styling solution** (utility-first). Global CSS is limited to Tailwind setup + the shared design system in `packages/ui-theme/styles.css`.

## Code Style Rules
- Naming conventions:
  - Files:
    - React components/pages: `PascalCase.tsx` (e.g. `Modal.tsx`, `AccountDetail.tsx`)
    - Non-component TS modules: `camelCase.ts` (e.g. `paymentUtils.ts`, `tokenValidation.ts`)
    - Types alongside a page: `Something.types.ts` (existing pattern: `AccountDetail.types.ts`)
  - Components: `PascalCase` function components (exported).
  - Hooks: `useSomething` (custom hooks only when extracted, otherwise keep local).
  - Functions/variables: `camelCase`; booleans as `isX/hasX/shouldX/canX`.
  - Constants: `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` for true constants (e.g. collection names).
- Preferred patterns:
  - **Functional components only**; prefer composition over inheritance/HOCs.
  - Keep “controller” logic in pages, isolate Firebase operations in `services/*`, keep pure logic in `utils/*`.
  - Use React built-ins for state: `useState`, `useEffect`, `useMemo`, `useCallback`; Context is primarily for auth.
  - URL state via React Router `useSearchParams` for filters/search.
- Import ordering (top → bottom):
  - React and core libs (`react`, `react-router*`)
  - Third-party libs (Firebase SDK, recharts, etc.)
  - Workspace packages (`@rates/*`)
  - Local absolute imports via alias (`@/*`)
  - Local relative imports (`./`, `../`)
  - Types: prefer `import type { ... }` when possible

## Tailwind CSS Rules (strict)
- ALWAYS use Tailwind utility classes for component styling.
- NEVER use inline styles (`style={{ ... }}`) unless absolutely necessary (document why).
- NEVER create new CSS files for component styling.
- Class ordering convention (enforce manually even if lint exists):
  - Position → Display → Sizing → Spacing → Typography → Colors → Borders → Effects → States
  - Example: `absolute flex w-full h-10 p-4 text-sm text-gray-800 bg-white border rounded-lg shadow-md hover:bg-gray-50`
- Conditional classes:
  - Use a `cn()` utility (recommended implementation: `clsx` + `tailwind-merge`) instead of ad-hoc string concatenation.
  - When adding variants, prefer **CVA (class-variance-authority)** + `cn()` to keep variants readable.
- Prefer Tailwind built-ins over arbitrary values (`[...]`). Only use arbitrary values when the design system cannot express it.
- Prefer theme values from Tailwind config (shared preset in `packages/ui-theme/tailwind.config.cjs`) over hardcoded colors/spacing.
- Responsive usage is **mobile-first**:
  - Base classes apply to mobile; add `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`, `xl:` overrides as needed.
- Dark mode:
  - If/when used, follow Tailwind conventions (`dark:` utilities). Do not introduce separate dark-mode CSS files.

